abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for deterministic
  demography, resource-constrained permanent household migration,
  evidence-grounded spatial experiments, and explicit temporary mobility and
  aggregation under declared model assumptions. Version 0.3.4 preserves the
  model-semantics-v25 state produced by the complete Scientific Audit v3
  remediation programme. Audit v3 interrogated the immutable v0.3.3/v21
  baseline across Areas A-N, demonstrated 17 findings (1 P0, 6 P1 and 10 P2),
  and all 17 were repaired, merged through protected CI, independently
  post-merge reverified, and closed before this release freeze. The v0.3.4
  baseline records that scientific-hardening state; it does not establish
  empirical archaeological validity or prove model correctness.
